{
  "title": "Last Night of Ramazan",
  "data": "Acts of the Night\nPerform ghusl tonight.\nVisit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.).\nRecite [Surah al-An'am](A10), [Surah al-Kahf](A22) and [Surah Ya-Sin](A40).\nRecite 100 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFIRULLAAHA WA ATOOBU ILAYH\nI implore for Allah’s forgiveness and I repent before Him.",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua Allahumma Hadha Shahru Ramadan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ وَقَدْ تَصَرَّمَ\nALLAAHUMMA HAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAANAL LADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AANA WA QAD TASARRAM\nO Allah, this month of Ramadan in which You revealed the Qur'an is about to come to its end.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِوَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ يَطْلُعَ الْفَجْرُ مِنْ لَيْلَتِيْ هٰذِهِ اَوْ يَتَصَرَّمَ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nWA A'OODHU BIWAJHIKAL KAREEMI YAA RABBI AN YATLU'AL FAJRU MIN LAYLATEE HAADHIHEE AW YATASARRAMA SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nI seek refuge with Your Noble Face, O Lord, that it dawns tonight or the month of Ramadan elapses\nوَلَكَ قِبَلِيْ تَبِعَةٌ اَوْ ذَنْبٌ تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تُعَذِّبَنِيْ بِهٖ يَوْمَ اَلْقَاكَ\nWA LAKA QIBALEE TABI'ATUN AW DHANBUN TUREEDU AN TU'ADHDHIBANEE BIHEE YAWMA ALQAAK\nbut I am still liable to an offense or a sin that You want to punish me for committing it when I will meet You.",
    "Dua Ya Mudabbir al-Umur\nيَا مُدَبِّرَ الْاُمُوْرِ، يَا بَاعِثَ مَنْ فِي الْقُبُوْرِ\nYAA MUDABBIRAL UMOORI YAA BAA'ITHA MAN FIL QUBOOR\nO Director of all affairs! O Resurrector of all those in graves!\nيَا مُجْرِيَ الْبُحُوْرِ يَا مُلَيِّنَ الْحَدِيْدِ لِدَاوُدَ\nYAA MUJRIYAL BUHOORI YAA MULAYYINAL HADEEDI LIDAAWUD\nO He Who causes oceans to flow; O He Who made the iron pliant for (Prophet) David\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(Please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَافْعَلْ بِي كَذا وَكَذا\nWAF'AL BEE KADHAA WA KADHAA\nAnd do for me (mention your legitimate desires)",
    "Sahifa Dua 45: Farewell to Ramazan\nBid farewell to the month of Ramazan with its farewell duas, such as al-Kulayni's [Farewell Prayer of Ramazan](AA47). The best of them may be this one:\nاللَّهُمَّ يَا مَنْ لَا يَرْغَبُ فِي الْجَزَاءِ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA MAN LAA YARGHABU FIL JAZAA'\nO God, O He who desires no repayment!\nوَيَا مَنْ لَا يَنْدَمُ عَلَى الْعَطَاءِ\nWA YAA MAN LAA YANDAMU A'LAL A'TAA'\nO He who shows no remorse at bestowal!\nوَيَا مَنْ لَا يُكَافِئُ عَبْدَهٗ عَلَى السَّوَاءِ\nWA YAA MAN LAA YUKAAFI'U A'BDAHOO A'LAS SAWAA'\nO He who rewards not His servant tit for tat!\nمِنَّتُكَ ابْتِدَاءٌ، وَعَفْوُكَ تَفَضُّلٌ\nMINNATUKAB TIDAA'UN WA A'FWUKA TAFADDUL\nYour kindness is a new beginning, Your pardon gratuitous bounty,\nوَعُقُوبَتُكَ عَدْلٌ، وَقَضَاؤُكَ خِيَرَةٌ\nWA U'QOOBATUKA A'DLUN WA QADAA'UKA KHIYARAH\nYour punishment justice, Your decree a choice for the best!\nاِنْ اَعْطَيْتَ لَمْ تَشُبْ عَطَاءَكَ بِمَنٍّ\nIN A'TAYTA LAM TASHUB A'TAA'AKA BIMANN\nIf You bestow, You stain not Your bestowal with obligation,\nوَاِنْ مَنَعْتَ لَمْ يَكُنْ مَنْعُكَ تَعَدِّياً\nWA IN MANA'TA LAM YAKUN MAN'UKA TA'ADDIYAA\nand if You withhold, You withhold not in transgression.\nتَشْكُرُ مَنْ شَكَرَكَ وَاَنْتَ اَلْهَمْتَهٗ شُكْرَكَ\nTASHKURU MAN SHAKARAKA WA ANTA ALHAMTAHOO SHUKRAK\nYou show gratitude to him who thanks You, while You have inspired him to thank You.\nوَتُكَافِئُ مَنْ حَمِدَكَ وَاَنْتَ عَلَّمْتَهٗ حَمْدَكَ\nWA TUKAAFI'U MAN HAMIDAKA WA ANTA A'LLAMTAHOO HAMDAK\nYou reward him who praises You, while though You have taught him Your praise.\nتَسْتُرُ عَلَى مَنْ لَوْ شِئْتَ فَضَحْتَهٗ\nTASTURU A'LAA MAN LAW SHI'TA FADAHTAH\nYou cover him whom, if You willed, You would expose,\nوَتَجُودُ عَلَى مَنْ لَوْ شِئْتَ مَنَعْتَهٗ\nWA TAJOODU A'LAA MAN LAW SHI'TA MANA'TAH\nand You are generous toward him from whom, if You willed, You would withhold.\nوَكِلَاهُمَا اَهْلٌ مِنْكَ لِلْفَضِيحَةِ وَالْمَنْعِ\nWA KILAAHUMAA AHLUN MINKA LIL FADEEHATI WAL MAN'\nBoth are worthy of Your exposure and withholding,\nغَيْرَ اَنَّكَ بَنَيْتَ اَفْعَالَكَ عَلَى التَّفَضُّلِ\nGHAYRA ANNAKA BANAYTA AF'AALAKA A'LAT TAFADDUL\nbut You have founded Your acts upon gratuitous bounty,\nوَاَجْرَيْتَ قُدْرَتَكَ عَلَى التَّجَاوُزِ\nWA AJRAYTA QUDRATAKA A'LAT TAJAAWUZ\nchannelled Your power into forbearance,\nوَتَلَقَّيْتَ مَنْ عَصَاكَ بِالْحِلْمِ\nWA TALAQQAYTA MAN A'SAAKA BIL HILM\nreceived him who disobeyed You with clemency,\nوَاَمْهَلْتَ مَنْ قَصَدَ لِنَفْسِهٖ بِالظُّلْمِ\nWA AMHALTA MAN QASADA LINAFSIHEE BIZ ZULM\nand disregarded him who intended wrongdoing against himself.\nتَسْتَنْظِرُهُمْ بِاَنَاتِكَ اِلَى الْاِنَابَةِ، وَتَتْرُكُ مُعَاجَلَتَهُمْ اِلَى التَّوْبَةِ\nTASTANZIRUHUM BI-ANAATIKA ILAL INAABATI WA TATRUKU MU'AAJALATAHUM ILAT TAWBAH\nYou await their turning back without haste and refrain from rushing them toward repentance,\nلِكَيْلَا يَهْلِكَ عَلَيْكَ هَالِكُهُمْ\nLIKAYLAA YAHLIKA A'LAYKA HAALIKUHUM\nso that the perisher among them may not perish because of You\nوَلَا يَشْقَى بِنِعْمَتِكَ شَقِيُّهُمْ\nWA LAA YASHQAA BINI'MATIKA SHAQIYYUHUM\nand the wretched may not be wretched through Your favour,\nاِلَّا عَنْ طُولِ الْاِعْذَارِ اِلَيْهِ\nILLAA A'N TOOLIL I'DHAARI ILAYH\nbut only after Your prolonged excusing him\nوَبَعْدَ تَرَادُفِ الْحُجَّةِ عَلَيْهِ\nWA BA'DA TARAADUFIL HUJJATI A'LAYH\nand successive arguments against him,\nكَرَماً مِنْ عَفْوِكَ يَا كَرِيمُ\nKARAMAN MIN A'FWIKA YAA KAREEM\nas an act of generosity through Your pardon, O Generous,\nوَعَائِدَةً مِنْ عَطْفِكَ يَا حَلِيمُ\nWA A'A'IDATAN MIN A'TFIKA YAA HALEEM\nand an act of kindliness through Your tenderness, O Clement!\nاَنْتَ الَّذِي فَتَحْتَ لِعِبَادِكَ بَاباً\nANTAL LADHEE FATAHTA LI-I'BAADIKA BAABAA\nIt is You who have opened for Your servants a door\nاِلَى عَفْوِكَ، وَسَمَّيْتَهُ التَّوْبَةَ\nILAA A'FWIKA WA SAMMAYTAHUT TAWBAH\nto Your pardon, which You have named 'repentance'.\nوَجَعَلْتَ عَلَى ذَلِكَ الْبَابِ دَلِيلًا مِنْ وَحْيِكَ\nWA JA'ALTA A'LAA DHAALIKAL BAABI DALEELAN MIN WAHYIK\nYou have placed upon that door a pointer from Your revelation,\nلِئَلَّا يَضِلُّوا عَنْهُ، فَقُلْتَ تَبَارَكَ اسْمُكَ\nLI-ALLAA YADILLOO A'NHU FAQULTA TABAARAKAS MUK\nlest they stray from it: You have said (blessed is Your Name),\nتُوبُوا اِلَى اللَّهِ تَوْبَةً نَصُوحاً عَسَى رَبُّكُمْ\nTOOBOO ILALLAAHI TAWBATAN NASOOHAN A'SAA RABBUKUM\n\"Repent toward God with unswerving repentance! It may be that Your Lord\nاَنْ يُكَفِّرَ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّئَاتِكُمْ وَيُدْخِلَكُمْ\nAN YUKAFFIRA A'NKUM SAYYI'AATIKUM WA YUDKHILAKUM\nwill acquit of your evil deeds and will admit you into\nجَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهَارُ\nJANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTIHAL ANHAAR\ngardens beneath which rivers flow,\nيَوْمَ لَا يُخْزِي اللَّهُ النَّبِيَّ\nYAWMA LAA YUKHZILLAAHUN NABIYY\nupon the day when God will not degrade the Prophet\nوَالَّذِينَ اٰمَنُوا مَعَهٗ، نُورُهُمْ يَسْعَى بَيْنَ اَيْدِيهِمْ وَبِاَيْمَانِهِمْ\nWAL LADHEENA AAMANOO MA'AHOO NOORUHUM YAS'AA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA BI-AYMAANIHIM\nand those who have faith along with him, their light running before them and on their right hands,\nيَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا اَتْمِمْ لَنَا نُورَنَا، وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا\nYAQOOLOONA RABBANAA ATMIM LANAA NOORANAA WAGHFIR LANAA\nand they say: 'Our Lord, complete for us our light, and forgive us!\nاِنَّكَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nSurely You are powerful over everything\" (66:8).\nفَمَا عُذْرُ مَنْ اَغْفَلَ دُخُولَ ذَلِكَ الْمَنْزِلِ\nFAMAA U'DHRU MAN AGHFALA DUKHOOLA DHAALIKAL MANZIL\nWhat is the excuse of him who remains heedless of entering that house\nبَعْدَ فَتْحِ الْبَابِ وَاِقَامَةِ الدَّلِيلِ\nBA'DA FAT-HIL BAABI WA IQAAMATID DALEEL\nafter the opening of the door and the setting up of the pointer?\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِي زِدْتَ فِي السَّوْمِ عَلَى نَفْسِكَ لِعِبَادِكَ\nWA ANTAL LADHEE ZIDTA FIS SAWMI A'LAA NAFSIKA LI-I'BAADIK\nIt is You who have raised the price against Yourself to the advantage of Your servants,\nتُرِيدُ رِبْحَهُمْ فِي مُتَاجَرَتِهِمْ لَكَ\nTUREEDU RIBHAHUM FEE MUTAAJARATIHIM LAK\ndesiring their profit in their trade with You,\nوَفَوْزَهُمْ بِالْوِفَادَةِ عَلَيْكَ، وَالزِّيَادَةِ مِنْكَ\nWA FAWZAHUM BIL WIFAADATI A'LAYKA WAZ ZIYAADATI MINK\ntheir triumph through reaching You, and their increase on account of You,\nفَقُلْتَ تَبَارَكَ اسْمُكَ وَتَعَالَيْتَ\nFAQULTA TABAARAKAS MUKA WA TA'AALAYT\nfor You have said (blessed is Your Name and high are You exalted),\nمَنْ جَاءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ عَشْرُ اَمْثَالِهَا\nMAN JAA'A BIL HASANATI FALAHOO A'SHRU AMTHAALIHAA\n\"Whoso brings a good deed shall have ten the like of it,\nوَمَنْ جَاءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزَى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا\nWA MAN JAA'A BIS SAYYI'ATI FALAA YUJZAA ILLAA MITHLAHAA\nand whoso brings an evil deed shall only be recompensed the like of it\" (6:160).\nوَقُلْتَ مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ\nWA QULTA MATHALUL LADHEENA YUNFIQOONA AMWAALAHUM FEE SABEELILLAAHI KAMATHALI HABBAH\nYou have said, \"The likeness of those who expend their wealth in the way of God is as the likeness of a grain of corn\nاَنْبَتَتْ سَبْعَ سَنَابِلَ فِي كُلِّ سُنْبُلَةٍ مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ\nANBATAT SAB'A SANAABILA FEE KULLI SUNBULATIN MI'ATU HABBAH\nthat sprouts seven ears, in every ear a hundred grains;\nوَاللَّهُ يُضَاعِفُ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ\nWALLAAHU YUDAA'IFU LIMAN YASHAA'\nso God multiplies unto whom He wills\" (2:261).\nوَقُلْتَ مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضاً حَسَناً\nWA QULTA MAN DHAL LADHEE YUQRIDULLAAHA QARDAN HASANAA\nYou have said, \"Who is he that will lend to God a good loan,\nفَيُضَاعِفَهٗ لَهٗ اَضْعَافاً كَثِيرَةً\nFAYUDAA'IFAHOO LAHOO AD'AAFAN KATHEERAH\nand He will multiply it for him manifold\" (2:245)?\nوَمَا اَنْزَلْتَ مِنْ نَظَائِرِهِنَّ فِي الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ تَضَاعِيفِ الْحَسَنَاتِ\nWA MAA ANZALTA MIN NAZAA'IRIHINNA FIL QUR'AANI MIN TADAA'EEFIL HASANAAT\nAnd You have sent down in the Qur'an similar verses on the multiplying of good deeds.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِي دَلَلْتَهُمْ بِقَوْلِكَ مِنْ غَيْبِكَ وَتَرْغِيبِكَ\nWA ANTAL LADHEE DALALTAHUM BIQAWLIKA MIN GHAYBIKA WA TARGHEEBIK\nIt is You who have pointed them through Your speech from Your Unseen and Your encouragement\nالَّذِي فِيهِ حَظُّهُمْ عَلَى مَا لَوْ سَتَرْتَهٗ عَنْهُمْ\nALLADHEE FEEHI HAZZUHUM A'LAA MAA LAW SATARTAHOO A'NHUM\nin which lies their good fortune toward that which - had You covered it from them\nلَمْ تُدْرِكْهُ اَبْصَارُهُمْ، وَلَمْ تَعِهٖ اَسْمَاعُهُمْ\nLAM TUDRIK-HU ABSAARUHUM WA LAM TA'IHEE ASMAA'UHUM\ntheir eyes would not have perceived, their ears would not have heard,\nوَلَمْ تَلْحَقْهُ اَوْهَامُهُمْ\nWA LAM TALHAQHU AWHAAMUHUM\nand their imaginations would not have grasped,\nفَقُلْتَ فَاذْكُرُونِي اَذْكُرْكُمْ، وَاشْكُرُوا لِي وَلَا تَكْفُرُونِ\nFAQULTA FADHKUROONEE ADHKURKUM WASHKUROO LEE WA LAA TAKFUROON\nfor You have said, \"Remember Me and I will remember you be thankful to Me, and be you not thankless towards Me\" (2:152)!\nوَقُلْتَ لَئِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ لَاَزِيدَنَّكُمْ\nWA QULTA LA-IN SHAKARTUM LA-AZEEDANNAKUM\nYou have said, \"If you are thankful, surely I will increase you,\nوَلَئِنْ كَفَرْتُمْ اِنَّ عَذَابِي لَشَدِيدٌ\nWA LA-IN KAFARTUM INNA A'DHAABEE LASHADEED\nbut if you are thankless, My chastisement is surely terrible\" (14:7);\nوَقُلْتَ ادْعُونِي اَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ\nWA QULTAD'OONEE ASTAJIB LAKUM\nAnd You have said, \"Supplicate Me and I will respond to you,\nاِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِي\nINNAL LADHEENA YASTAKBIROONA A'N I'BAADATEE\nsurely those who wax too proud to worship Me\nسَيَدْخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ\nSAYADKHULOONA JAHANNAMA DAAKHIREEN\nshall enter Gehenna utterly abject\" (40:60).\nفَسَمَّيْتَ دُعَاءَكَ عِبَادَةً، وَتَرْكَهُ اسْتِكْبَاراً\nFASAMMAYTA DU'AA'AKA I'BAADATAN WA TARKAHUS TIKBAARAA\nHence You have named supplicating You 'worship' and refraining from it 'waxing proud',\nوَتَوَعَّدْتَ عَلَى تَرْكِهٖ دُخُولَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ\nWA TAWA''ADTA A'LAA TARKIHEE DUKHOOLA JAHANNAMA DAAKHIREEN\nand You have threatened that the refraining from it would yield entrance into Gehenna in utter abjection.\nفَذَكَرُوكَ بِمَنِّكَ، وَشَكَرُوكَ بِفَضْلِكَ\nFADHAKAROOKA BIMANNIKA WA SHAKAROOKA BIFADLIK\nSo they remember You for Your kindness, they thank You for Your bounty,\nوَدَعَوْكَ بِاَمْرِكَ\nWA DA'AWKA BI-AMRIK\nthey supplicate You by Your command,\nوَتَصَدَّقُوا لَكَ طَلَباً لِمَزِيدِكَ\nWA TASADDAQOO LAKA TALABAN LIMAZEEDIK\nand they donate for You in order to seek Your increase;\nوَفِيهَا كَانَتْ نَجَاتُهُمْ مِنْ غَضَبِكَ\nWA FEEHAA KAANAT NAJAATUHUM MIN GHADABIK\nin all this lies their deliverance from Your wrath\nوَفَوْزُهُمْ بِرِضَاكَ\nWA FAWZUHUM BIRIDAAK\nand their triumph through Your good pleasure.\nوَلَوْ دَلَّ مَخْلُوقٌ مَخْلُوقاً مِنْ نَفْسِهٖ\nWA LAW DALLA MAKHLOOQUN MAKHLOOQAN MIN NAFSIH\nWere any creature himself to direct another creature\nعَلَى مِثْلِ الَّذِي دَلَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عِبَادَكَ مِنْكَ\nA'LAA MITHLIL LADHEE DALALTA A'LAYHI I'BAADAKA MINK\nto the like of that to which You Yourself have directed Your servants,\nكَانَ مَوْصُوفاً بِالْاِحْسَانِ\nKAANA MAWSOOFAN BIL IHSAAN\nhe would be described by beneficence,\nوَمَنْعُوتاً بِالِامْتِنَانِ، وَمَحْمُوداً بِكُلِّ لِسَانٍ\nWA MAN'OOTAN BIL IMTINAANI WA MAHMOODAN BIKULLI LISAAN\nqualified by kindness, and praised by every tongue.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ مَا وُجِدَ فِي حَمْدِكَ مَذْهَبٌ\nFALAKAL HAMDU MAA WUJIDA FEE HAMDIKA MADH-HAB\nSo to You belongs praise as long as there is found a way to praise You\nوَمَا بَقِيَ لِلْحَمْدِ لَفْظٌ تُحْمَدُ بِهٖ، وَمَعْنًى يَنْصَرِفُ اِلَيْهِ\nWA MAA BAQIYA LIL HAMDI LAFZUN TUHMADU BIHEE WA MA'NAN YANSARIFU ILAYH\nand as long as there remains for praising words by which You may be praised and meanings which may be spent in praise!\nيَا مَنْ تَحَمَّدَ اِلَى عِبَادِهٖ بِالْاِحْسَانِ وَالْفَضْلِ\nYAA MAN TAHAMMADA ILAA I'BAADIHEE BIL IHSAANI WAL FADL\nO He who shows Himself praiseworthy to His servants through beneficence and bounty,\nوَغَمَرَهُمْ بِالْمَنِّ وَالطَّوْلِ\nWA GHAMARAHUM BIL MANNI WAT TAWL\nflooding them with kindness and graciousness!\nمَا اَفْشَى فِينَا نِعْمَتَكَ، وَاَسْبَغَ عَلَيْنَا مِنَّتَكَ\nMAA AFSHAA FEENAA NI'MATAKA WA ASBAGHA A'LAYNAA MINNATAK\nHow much Your favour has been spread about among us, Your kindness lavished upon us,\nوَاَخَصَّنَا بِبِرِّكَ\nWA AKHASSANAA BIBIRRIK\nand Your goodness singled out for us!\nهَدَيْتَنَا لِدِينِكَ الَّذِي اصْطَفَيْتَ\nHADAYTANAA LIDEENIKAL LADHIS TAFAYT\nYou have guided us to Your religion which You have chosen,\nوَمِلَّتِكَ الَّتِي ارْتَضَيْتَ\nWA MILLATIKAL LATIR TADAYT\nYour creed with which You are pleased,\nوَسَبِيلِكَ الَّذِي سَهَّلْتَ\nWA SABEELIKAL LADHEE SAHHALT\nand Your path which You have made smooth,\nوَبَصَّرْتَنَا الزُّلْفَةَ لَدَيْكَ، وَالْوُصُولَ اِلَى كَرَامَتِكَ\nWA BASSARTANAZ ZULFATA LADAYKA WAL WUSOOLA ILAA KARAAMATIK\nand You have shown us proximity to You and arrival at Your generosity!\nاللَّهُمَّ وَاَنْتَ جَعَلْتَ مِنْ صَفَايَا تِلْكَ الْوَظَائِفِ\nALLAAHUMMA WA ANTA JA'ALTA MIN SAFAAYAA TILKAL WAZAA'IF\nO God, You have appointed among the choicest of those duties\nوَخَصَائِصِ تِلْكَ الْفُرُوضِ\nWA KHASAA'ISI TILKAL FUROOD\nand the most special of those obligations\nشَهْرَ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِي اخْتَصَصْتَهٗ مِنْ سَائِرِ الشُّهُورِ\nSHAHRA RAMADAANAL LADHIKH TASASTAHOO MIN SAA'IRISH SHUHOOR\nthe month of Ramadan, which You have singled out from other months,\nوَتَخَيَّرْتَهٗ مِنْ جَمِيعِ الْاَزْمِنَةِ وَالدُّهُورِ\nWA TAKHAYYARTAHOO MIN JAMEE'IL AZMINATI WAD DUHOOR\nchosen from among all periods and eras,\nوَاٰثَرْتَهٗ عَلَى كُلِّ اَوْقَاتِ السَّنَةِ\nWA AATHARTAHOO A'LAA KULLI AWQAATIS SANAH\nand preferred over all times of the year\nبِمَا اَنْزَلْتَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ وَالنُّورِ\nBIMAA ANZALTA FEEHI MINAL QUR'AANI WAN NOOR\nthrough the Qur'an and the Light which You sent down within it,\nوَضَاعَفْتَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْاِيمَانِ\nWA DAA'AFTA FEEHI MINAL EEMAAN\nthe faith which You multiplied by means of it,\nوَفَرَضْتَ فِيهِ مِنَ الصِّيَامِ\nWA FARADTA FEEHI MINAS SIYAAM\nthe fasting which You obligated therein,\nوَرَغَّبْتَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْقِيَامِ\nWA RAGHGHABTA FEEHI MINAL QIYAAM\nthe standing in prayer which You encouraged at its time,\nوَاَجْلَلْتَ فِيهِ مِنْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ\nWA AJLALTA FEEHI MIN LAYLATIL QADR\nand the Night of Decree which You magnified therein,\nالَّتِي هِيَ خَيْرٌ مِنْ اَلْفِ شَهْرٍ\nALLATEE HIYA KHAYRUN MIN ALFI SHAHR\nthe night which is \"better than a thousand months\" (97:3).\nثُمَّ اٰثَرْتَنَا بِهٖ عَلَى سَائِرِ الْاُمَمِ\nTHUMMA AATHARTANAA BIHEE A'LAA SAA'IRIL UMAM\nThrough it You have preferred us over the other communities\nوَاصْطَفَيْتَنَا بِفَضْلِهٖ دُونَ اَهْلِ الْمِلَلِ\nWASTAFAYTANAA BIFADLIHEE DOONA AHLIL MILAL\nand through its excellence You have chosen us to the exclusion of the people of the creeds.\nفَصُمْنَا بِاَمْرِكَ نَهَارَهٗ\nFASUMNAA BI-AMRIKA NAHAARAH\nWe fasted by Your command in its daylight,\nوَقُمْنَا بِعَوْنِكَ لَيْلَهٗ\nWA QUMNAA BI-A'WNIKA LAYLAH\nwe stood in prayer with Your help in its night,\nمُتَعَرِّضِينَ بِصِيَامِهٖ وَقِيَامِهٖ لِمَا عَرَّضْتَنَا لَهٗ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ\nMUTA'ARRIDEENA BISIYAAMIHEE WA QIYAAMIHEE LIMAA A'RRADTANAA LAHOO MIN RAHMATIK\npresenting ourselves by its fasting and its standing to the mercy which You have held up before us,\nوَتَسَبَّبْنَا اِلَيْهِ مِنْ مَثُوبَتِكَ\nWA TASABBABNAA ILAYHI MIN MATHOOBATIK\nand we found through it the means to Your reward.\nوَاَنْتَ الْمَلِيءُ بِمَا رُغِبَ فِيهِ اِلَيْكَ\nWA ANTAL MALEE'U BIMAA RUGHIBA FEEHI ILAYK\nAnd You are full of what is sought from You,\nالْجَوَادُ بِمَا سُئِلْتَ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ\nAL-JAWAADU BIMAA SU'ILTA MIN FADLIK\nmunificent with what is asked of Your bounty,\nالْقَرِيبُ اِلَى مَنْ حَاوَلَ قُرْبَكَ\nAL-QAREEBU ILAA MAN HAAWALA QURBAK\nand near to him who strives for Your nearness.\nوَقَدْ اَقَامَ فِينَا هَذَا الشَّهْرُ مُقَامَ حَمْدٍ\nWA QAD AQAAMA FEENAA HAADHASH SHAHRU MUQAAMA HAMD\nThis month stood among us in a standing place of praise,\nوَصَحِبَنَا صُحْبَةَ مَبْرُورٍ\nWA SAHIBANAA SUHBATA MABROOR\naccompanied us with the companionship of one approved,\nوَاَرْبَحَنَا اَفْضَلَ اَرْبَاحِ الْعَالَمِينَ\nWA ARBAHANAA AFDALA ARBAAHIL A'ALAMEEN\nand profited us with the most excellent profit of the world's creatures.\nثُمَّ قَدْ فَارَقَنَا عِنْدَ تَمَامِ وَقْتِهٖ، وَانْقِطَاعِ مُدَّتِهٖ، وَوَفَاءِ عَدَدِهٖ\nTHUMMA QAD FAARAQANAA I'NDA TAMAAMI WAQTIHEE WANQITAA'I MUDDATIHEE WA WAFAA'I A'DADIH\nThen it parted from us at the completion of its time, the end of its term, and the fulfilment of its number.\nفَنَحْنُ مُوَدِّعُوهُ وِدَاعَ مَنْ عَزَّ فِرَاقُهٗ عَلَيْنَا\nFANAHNU MUWADDI'OOHU WIDAA'A MAN A'ZZA FIRAAQUHOO A'LAYNAA\nSo we bid farewell to it with the farewell of one whose parting pains us,\nوَغَمَّنَا وَاَوْحَشَنَا انْصِرَافُهٗ عَنَّا\nWA GHAMMANAA WA AWHASHANAN SIRAAFUHOO A'NNAA\nwhose leaving fills us with gloom and loneliness,\nوَلَزِمَنَا لَهُ الذِّمَامُ الْمَحْفُوظُ\nWA LAZIMANAA LAHUDH DHIMAAMUL MAHFOOZ\nand to whom we have come to owe a safeguarded claim,\nوَالْحُرْمَةُ الْمَرْعِيَّةُ، وَالْحَقُّ الْمَقْضِيُّ\nWAL HURMATUL MAR'IYYATU WAL HAQQUL MAQDIYY\nan observed inviolability, and a discharged right.\nفَنَحْنُ قَائِلُونَ السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ\nFANAHNU QAA'ILOONAS SALAAMU A'LAYK\nWe say: Peace be upon You,\nيَا شَهْرَ اللَّهِ الْاَكْبَرَ، وَيَا عِيدَ اَوْلِيَائِهِ\nYAA SHAHRALLAAHIL AKBARA WA YAA I'EEDA AWLIYAA'IH\nO greatest month of God! O festival of His friends!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَكْرَمَ مَصْحُوبٍ مِنَ الْاَوْقَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AKRAMA MAS-HOOBIN MINAL AWQAAT\nPeace be upon You, O most noble of accompanying times!\nوَيَا خَيْرَ شَهْرٍ فِي الْاَيَّامِ وَالسَّاعَاتِ\nWA YAA KHAYRA SHAHRIN FIL AYYAAMI WAS SAA'AAT\nO best of months in days and hours!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ شَهْرٍ قَرُبَتْ فِيهِ الْاٰمَالُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN SHAHRIN QARUBAT FEEHIL AAMAAL\nPeace be upon You, month in which expectations come near\nوَنُشِرَتْ فِيهِ الْاَعْمَالُ\nWA NUSHIRAT FEEHIL A'MAAL\nand good works are scattered about!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَرِينٍ جَلَّ قَدْرُهٗ مَوْجُوداً\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN QAREENIN JALLA QADRUHOO MAWJOODAA\nPeace be upon You, comrade who is great in worth when found\nوَاَفْجَعَ فَقْدُهٗ مَفْقُوداً، وَمَرْجُوٍّ اٰلَمَ فِرَاقُهُ\nWA AFJA'A FAQDUHOO MAFQOODAN WA MARJUWWIN AALAMA FIRAAQUH\nand who torments through absence when lost, anticipated friend whose parting gives pain!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَلِيفٍ اٰنَسَ مُقْبِلًا فَسَرَّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN ALEEFIN AANASA MUQBILAN FASARR\nPeace be upon You, familiar who brought comfort in coming, thus making happy,\nوَاَوْحَشَ مُنْقَضِياً فَمَضَّ\nWA AWHASHA MUNQADIYAN FAMADD\nwho left loneliness in going, thus giving anguish!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ مُجَاوِرٍ رَقَّتْ فِيهِ الْقُلُوبُ، وَقَلَّتْ فِيهِ الذُّنُوبُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN MUJAAWIRIN RAQQAT FEEHIL QULOOBU WA QALLAT FEEHIDH DHUNOOB\nPeace be upon You, neighbour in whom hearts became tender and sins became few!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ نَاصِرٍ اَعَانَ عَلَى الشَّيْطَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN NAASIRIN A'AANA A'LASH SHAYTAAN\nPeace be upon You, helper who aided against Satan,\nوَصَاحِبٍ سَهَّلَ سُبُلَ الْاِحْسَانِ\nWA SAAHIBIN SAHHALA SUBULAL IHSAAN\ncompanion who made easy the paths of good-doing!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مَا اَكْثَرَ عُتَقَاءَ اللَّهِ فِيكَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MAA AKTHARA U'TAQAA'ALLAAHI FEEK\nPeace be upon You - How many became freedmen of God within You!\nوَمَا اَسْعَدَ مَنْ رَعَى حُرْمَتَكَ بِكَ\nWA MAA AS'ADA MAN RA'AA HURMATAKA BIK\nHow happy those who observed the respect due to You!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مَا كَانَ اَمْحَاكَ لِلذُّنُوبِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MAA KAANA AMHAAKA LIDH DHUNOOB\nPeace be upon You - How many the sins You erased!\nوَاَسْتَرَكَ لِاَنْوَاعِ الْعُيُوبِ\nWA ASTARAKA LI-ANWAA'IL U'YOOB\nHow many the kinds of faults You covered over!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مَا كَانَ اَطْوَلَكَ عَلَى الْمُجْرِمِينَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MAA KAANA ATWALAKA A'LAL MUJRIMEEN\nPeace be upon You - How drawn out were You for the sinners!\nوَاَهْيَبَكَ فِي صُدُورِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nWA AHYABAKA FEE SUDOORIL MU'MINEEN\nHow awesome were You in the hearts of the faithful!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ شَهْرٍ لَا تُنَافِسُهُ الْاَيَّامُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN SHAHRIN LAA TUNAAFISUHUL AYYAAM\nPeace be upon You, month with which no days compete!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ شَهْرٍ هُوَ مِنْ كُلِّ اَمْرٍ سَلَامٌ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN SHAHRIN HUWA MIN KULLI AMRIN SALAAM\nPeace be upon You, month which is peace in all affairs!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ غَيْرَ كَرِيهِ الْمُصَاحَبَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA GHAYRA KAREEHIL MUSAAHABAH\nPeace be upon You, You whose companionship is not disliked,\nوَلَا ذَمِيمِ الْمُلَابَسَةِ\nWA LAA DHAMEEMIL MULAABASAH\nYou whose friendly mixing is not blamed!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ كَمَا وَفَدْتَ عَلَيْنَا بِالْبَرَكَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA KAMAA WAFADTA A'LAYNAA BIL BARAKAAT\nPeace be upon You, just as You have entered upon us with blessings\nوَغَسَلْتَ عَنَّا دَنَسَ الْخَطِيئَاتِ\nWA GHASALTA A'NNAA DANASAL KHATEE'AAT\nand cleansed us of the defilement of offenses!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ غَيْرَ مُوَدَّعٍ بَرَماً\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA GHAYRA MUWADDA'IN BARAMAA\nPeace be upon You - You are not bid farewell in annoyance\nوَلَا مَتْرُوكٍ صِيَامُهٗ سَاَماً\nWA LAA MATROOKIN SIYAAMUHOO SA'AMAA\nnor is Your fasting left in weariness!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ مَطْلُوبٍ قَبْلَ وَقْتِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN MATLOOBIN QABLA WAQTIH\nPeace be upon You, object of seeking before Your time,\nوَمَحْزُونٍ عَلَيْهِ قَبْلَ فَوْتِهِ\nWA MAHZOONIN A'LAYHI QABLA FAWTIH\nobject of sorrow before Your passing!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ كَمْ مِنْ سُوءٍ صُرِفَ بِكَ عَنَّا\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA KAM MIN SOO'IN SURIFA BIKA A'NNAA\nPeace be upon You - How much evil was turned away from us through You!\nوَكَمْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ اُفِيضَ بِكَ عَلَيْنَا\nWA KAM MIN KHAYRIN UFEEDA BIKA A'LAYNAA\nHow much good flowed upon us because of You!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَى لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA LAYLATIL QADR\nPeace be upon You and upon the Night of Decree\nالَّتِي هِيَ خَيْرٌ مِنْ اَلْفِ شَهْرٍ\nALLATEE HIYA KHAYRUN MIN ALFI SHAHR\nwhich is \"better than a thousand months\" (97:3)!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مَا كَانَ اَحْرَصَنَا بِالْاَمْسِ عَلَيْكَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MAA KAANA AHRASANAA BIL AMSI A'LAYK\nPeace be upon You - How much we craved You yesterday!\nوَاَشَدَّ شَوْقَنَا غَداً اِلَيْكَ\nWA ASHADDA SHAWQANAA GHADAN ILAYK\nHow intensely we shall yearn for You tomorrow!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَى فَضْلِكَ الَّذِي حُرِمْنَاهُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA FADLIKAL LADHEE HURIMNAAH\nPeace be upon You and upon Your bounty which has now been made unlawful to us\nوَعَلَى مَاضٍ مِنْ بَرَكَاتِكَ سُلِبْنَاهُ\nWA A'LAA MAADIN MIN BARAKAATIKA SULIBNAAH\nand upon Your blessings gone by which have now been stripped away from us!\nاللَّهُمَّ اِنَّا اَهْلُ هَذَا الشَّهْرِ الَّذِي شَرَّفْتَنَا بِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA AHLU HAADHASH SHAHRIL LADHEE SHARRAFTANAA BIH\nO God, we are the people of this month. Through it You have ennobled us\nوَوَفَّقْتَنَا بِمَنِّكَ لَهٗ حِينَ جَهِلَ الْاَشْقِيَاءُ وَقْتَهٗ\nWA WAFFAQTANAA BIMANNIKA LAHOO HEENA JAHILAL ASHQIYAA'U WAQTAH\nand given us success because of Your kindness, while the wretched are ignorant of its time.\nوَحُرِمُوا لِشَقَائِهِمْ فَضْلَهٗ\nWA HURIMOO LISHAQAA'IHIM FADLAH\nMade unlawful to them is its bounty because of their wretchedness.\nاَنْتَ وَلِيُّ مَا اٰثَرْتَنَا بِهٖ مِنْ مَعْرِفَتِهٖ\nANTA WALIYYU MAA AATHARTANAA BIHEE MIN MA'RIFATIH\nYou are the patron of the knowledge of it by which You have preferred us,\nوَهَدَيْتَنَا لَهٗ مِنْ سُنَّتِهٖ\nWA HADAYTANAA LAHOO MIN SUNNATIH\nand its prescribed practices to which You have guided us.\nوَقَدْ تَوَلَّيْنَا بِتَوْفِيقِكَ صِيَامَهٗ وَقِيَامَهٗ عَلَى تَقْصِيرٍ\nWA QAD TAWALLAYNAA BITAWFEEQIKA SIYAAMAHOO WA QIYAAMAHOO A'LAA TAQSEER\nWe have undertaken, through Your giving success, its fasting and its standing in prayer, but with shortcomings,\nوَاَدَّيْنَا فِيهِ قَلِيلًا مِنْ كَثِيرٍ\nWA ADDAYNAA FEEHI QALEELAN MIN KATHEER\nand we have performed little of much.\nاللَّهُمَّ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ اِقْرَاراً بِالْاِسَاءَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA FALAKAL HAMDU IQRAARAN BIL ISAA'AH\nO God, so to You belongs praise, in admission of evil doing\nوَاعْتِرَافاً بِالْاِضَاعَةِ، وَلَكَ مِنْ قُلُوبِنَا عَقْدُ النَّدَمِ\nWA'TIRAAFAN BIL IDAA'ATI WA LAKA MIN QULOOBINAA A'QDUN NADAM\nand confession of negligence, and to You belongs remorse firmly knitted in our hearts\nوَمِنْ اَلْسِنَتِنَا صِدْقُ الِاعْتِذَارِ\nWA MIN ALSINATINAA SIDQUL I'TIDHAAR\nand seeking of pardon sincerely uttered by our tongues.\nفَاْجُرْنَا عَلَى مَا اَصَابَنَا فِيهِ مِنَ التَّفْرِيطِ\nFA'JURNAA A'LAA MAA ASAABANAA FEEHI MINAT TAFREET\nReward us, in spite of the neglect that befell us in this month,\nاَجْراً نَسْتَدْرِكُ بِهِ الْفَضْلَ الْمَرْغُوبَ فِيهِ\nAJRAN NASTADRIKU BIHIL FADLAL MARGHOOBA FEEH\nwith a reward through which we may reach the bounty desired from it\nوَنَعْتَاضُ بِهٖ مِنْ اَنْوَاعِ الذُّخْرِ الْمَحْرُوصِ عَلَيْهِ\nWA NA'TAADU BIHEE MIN ANWAA'IDH DHUKHRIL MAHROOSI A'LAYH\nand win the varieties of its craved stores!\nوَاَوْجِبْ لَنَا عُذْرَكَ عَلَى مَا قَصَّرْنَا فِيهِ مِنْ حَقِّكَ\nWA AWJIB LANAA U'DHRAKA A'LAA MAA QASSARNAA FEEHI MIN HAQQIK\nMake incumbent upon us Your pardon for our falling short of Your right in this month\nوَابْلُغْ بِاَعْمَارِنَا مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِينَا مِنْ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ الْمُقْبِلِ\nWABLUGH BI-A'MAARINAA MAA BAYNA AYDEENAA MIN SHAHRI RAMADAANAL MUQBIL\nand make our lives which lie before us reach the coming month of Ramadan!\nفَاِذَا بَلَّغْتَنَاهُ فَاَعِنَّا عَلَى تَنَاوُلِ\nFA-IDHAA BALLAGHTANAAHU FA-A'INNAA A'LAA TANAAWUL\nOnce You have made us reach it, help us perform\nمَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ مِنَ الْعِبَادَةِ\nMAA ANTA AHLUHOO MINAL I'BAADAH\nthe worship of which You are worthy,\nوَاَدِّنَا اِلَى الْقِيَامِ بِمَا يَسْتَحِقُّهٗ مِنَ الطَّاعَةِ\nWA ADDINAA ILAL QIYAAMI BIMAA YASTAHIQQUHOO MINAT TAA'AH\ncause us to undertake the obedience which You deserve,\nوَاَجْرِ لَنَا مِنْ صَالِحِ الْعَمَلِ\nWA AJRI LANAA MIN SAALIHIL A'MAL\nand grant us righteous works\nمَا يَكُونُ دَرَكاً لِحَقِّكَ فِي الشَّهْرَيْنِ مِنْ شُهُورِ الدَّهْرِ\nMAA YAKOONU DARAKAN LIHAQQIKA FISH SHAHRAYNI MIN SHUHOORID DAHR\nthat we may fulfil Your right in these two months of the months of time.\nاللَّهُمَّ وَمَا اَلْمَمْنَا بِهٖ فِي شَهْرِنَا هَذَا مِنْ لَمَمٍ اَوْ اِثْمٍ\nALLAAHUMMA WA MAA ALMAMNAA BIHEE FEE SHAHRINAA HAADHAA MIN LAMAMIN AW ITHM\nO God, as for the small and large sins which we have committed in this our month,\nاَوْ وَاقَعْنَا فِيهِ مِنْ ذَنْبٍ، وَاكْتَسَبْنَا فِيهِ مِنْ خَطِيئَةٍ\nAW WAAQA'NAA FEEHI MIN DHANBIN WAKTASABNAA FEEHI MIN KHATEE'AH\nthe misdeeds into which we have fallen, and the offenses which we have earned\nعَلَى تَعَمُّدٍ مِنَّا، اَوْ عَلَى نِسْيَانٍ ظَلَمْنَا فِيهِ اَنْفُسَنَا، اَوِ انْتَهَكْنَا بِهٖ حُرْمَةً مِنْ غَيْرِنَا\nA'LAA TA'AMMUDIN MINNAA AW A'LAA NISYAANIN ZALAMNAA FEEHI ANFUSANAA AWIN TAHAKNAA BIHEE HURMATAN MIN GHAYRINAA\npurposefully or in forgetfulness, wronging ourselves thereby or violating the respect due to others,\nفَصَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ، وَاسْتُرْنَا بِسِتْرِكَ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WASTURNAA BISITRIK\nbless Muhammad and his Household, cover us over with Your covering,\nوَاعْفُ عَنَّا بِعَفْوِكَ\nWA'FU A'NNAA BI-A'FWIK\npardon us through Your pardoning,\nوَلَا تَنْصِبْنَا فِيهِ لِاَعْيُنِ الشَّامِتِينَ\nWA LAA TANSIBNAA FEEHI LI-A'YUNISH SHAAMITEEN\nplace us not before the eyes of the gloaters because of that,\nوَلَا تَبْسُطْ عَلَيْنَا فِيهِ اَلْسُنَ الطَّاعِنِينَ\nWA LAA TABSUT A'LAYNAA FEEHI ALSUNAT TAA'INEEN\nstretch not toward us the tongues of the defamers,\nوَاسْتَعْمِلْنَا بِمَا يَكُونُ حِطَّةً وَكَفَّارَةً\nWASTA'MILNAA BIMAA YAKOONU HITTATAN WA KAFFAARAH\nand employ us in that which will alleviate and expiate\nلِمَا اَنْكَرْتَ مِنَّا فِيهِ بِرَاْفَتِكَ الَّتِي لَا تَنْفَدُ\nLIMAA ANKARTA MINNAA FEEHI BIRA'FATIKAL LATEE LAA TANFAD\nwhatever You disapprove from us within it through Your clemency which does not run out,\nوَفَضْلِكَ الَّذِي لَا يَنْقُصُ\nWA FADLIKAL LADHEE LAA YANQUS\nand Your bounty which does not diminish!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاجْبُرْ مُصِيبَتَنَا بِشَهْرِنَا\nWAJBUR MUSEEBATANAA BISHAHRINAA\nredress our being afflicted by our month,\nوَبَارِكْ لَنَا فِي يَوْمِ عِيدِنَا وَفِطْرِنَا\nWA BAARIK LANAA FEE YAWMI I'EEDINAA WA FITRINAA\nbless us in this day of our festival and our fast-breaking,\nوَاجْعَلْهُ مِنْ خَيْرِ يَوْمٍ مَرَّ عَلَيْنَا اَجْلَبِهٖ لِعَفْوٍ، وَاَمْحَاهُ لِذَنْبٍ\nWAJ'ALHU MIN KHAYRI YAWMIN MARRA A'LAYNAA AJLABIHEE LI-A'FWIN WA AMHAAHU LIDHANB\nmake it one of the best of days that have passed over us, the greatest in attracting Your pardon, and the most effacing toward sins,\nوَاغْفِرْ لَنَا مَا خَفِيَ مِنْ ذُنُوبِنَا وَمَا عَلَنَ\nWAGHFIR LANAA MAA KHAFIYA MIN DHUNOOBINAA WA MAA A'LAN\nand forgive us our sins, both the concealed and the public!\nاللَّهُمَّ اسْلَخْنَا بِانْسِلَاخِ هَذَا الشَّهْرِ مِنْ خَطَايَانَا\nALLAAHUMMAS LAKHNAA BINSILAAKHI HAADHASH SHAHRI MIN KHATAAYAANAA\nO God, with the passing of this month make us pass forth from our offenses,\nوَاَخْرِجْنَا بِخُرُوجِهٖ مِنْ سَيِّئَاتِنَا\nWA AKHRIJNAA BIKHUROOJIHEE MIN SAYYI'AATINAA\nwith its departure make us depart from our evil deeds,\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنْ اَسْعَدِ اَهْلِهٖ بِهٖ\nWAJ'ALNAA MIN AS'ADI AHLIHEE BIH\nand appoint us thereby among its most felicitous people,\nوَاَجْزَلِهِمْ قِسْماً فِيهِ، وَاَوْفَرِهِمْ حَظّاً مِنْهُ\nWA AJZALIHIM QISMAN FEEHI WA AWFARIHIM HAZZAN MINH\nthe most plentiful of them in portion, and the fullest of them in share!\nاللَّهُمَّ وَمَنْ رَعَى هَذَا الشَّهْرَ حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA WA MAN RA'AA HAADHASH SHAHRA HAQQA RI'AAYATIH\nO God, when any person observes this month as it should be observed,\nوَحَفِظَ حُرْمَتَهٗ حَقَّ حِفْظِهَا، وَقَامَ بِحُدُودِهٖ حَقَّ قِيَامِهَا\nWA HAFIZA HURMATAHOO HAQQA HIFZIHAA WA QAAMA BIHUDOODIHEE HAQQA QIYAAMIHAA\nsafeguards its inviolability as it should be safeguarded, attends to its bounds as they should be attended to,\nوَاتَّقَى ذُنُوبَهٗ حَقَّ تُقَاتِهَا، اَوْ تَقَرَّبَ اِلَيْكَ بِقُرْبَةٍ\nWATTAQAA DHUNOOBAHOO HAQQA TUQAATIHAA AW TAQARRABA ILAYKA BIQURBAH\nfears its misdeeds as they should be feared, or seeks nearness to You with any act of nearness-seeking\nاَوْجَبَتْ رِضَاكَ لَهٗ، وَعَطَفَتْ رَحْمَتَكَ عَلَيْهِ\nAWJABAT RIDAAKA LAHOO WA A'TAFAT RAHMATAKA A'LAYH\nwhich makes incumbent upon him Your good pleasure and bends toward him Your mercy,\nفَهَبْ لَنَا مِثْلَهٗ مِنْ وُجْدِكَ\nFAHAB LANAA MITHLAHOO MIN WUJDIK\ngive to us the like [of that] from Your wealth\nوَاَعْطِنَا اَضْعَافَهٗ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ\nWA A'TINAA AD'AAFAHOO MIN FADLIK\nand bestow it upon us in multiples through Your bounty,\nفَاِنَّ فَضْلَكَ لَا يَغِيضُ، وَاِنَّ خَزَائِنَكَ لَا تَنْقُصُ بَلْ تَفِيضُ\nFA-INNA FADLAKA LAA YAGHEEDU WA INNA KHAZAA'INAKA LAA TANQUSU BAL TAFEED\nfor Your bounty does not diminish, Your treasuries do not decrease but overflow,\nوَاِنَّ مَعَادِنَ اِحْسَانِكَ لَا تَفْنَى\nWA INNA MA'AADINA IHSAANIKA LAA TAFNAA\nthe mines of Your beneficence are not exhausted,\nوَاِنَّ عَطَاءَكَ لَلْعَطَاءُ الْمُهَنَّا\nWA INNA A'TAA'AKA LAL A'TAA'UL MUHANNAA\nand Your bestowal is the bestowal full of delight!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household\nوَاكْتُبْ لَنَا مِثْلَ اُجُورِ مَنْ صَامَهٗ\nWAKTUB LANAA MITHLA UJOORI MAN SAAMAH\nand write for us the like of the wages of him who fasted in it\nاَوْ تَعَبَّدَ لَكَ فِيهِ اِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ\nAW TA'ABBADA LAKA FEEHI ILAA YAWMIL QIYAAMAH\nor worshipped You within it until the Day of Resurrection!\nاللَّهُمَّ اِنَّا نَتُوبُ اِلَيْكَ فِي يَوْمِ فِطْرِنَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA NATOOBU ILAYKA FEE YAWMI FITRINAA\nO God, we repent to You in our day of fast-breaking,\nالَّذِي جَعَلْتَهٗ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ عِيداً وَسُرُوراً\nALLADHEE JA'ALTAHOO LIL MU'MINEENA I'EEDAN WA SUROORAA\nwhich You have appointed for the faithful a festival and a joy\nوَلِاَهْلِ مِلَّتِكَ مَجْمَعاً وَمُحْتَشَداً مِنْ كُلِّ ذَنْبٍ اَذْنَبْنَاهُ\nWA LI-AHLI MILLATIKA MAJMA'AN WA MUHTASHADAN MIN KULLI DHANBIN ADHNABNAAH\nand for the people of Your creed a time of assembly and gathering, from every misdeed we did,\nاَوْ سُوءٍ اَسْلَفْنَاهُ، اَوْ خَاطِرِ شَرٍّ اَضْمَرْنَاهُ\nAW SOO'IN ASLAFNAAHU AW KHAATIRI SHARRIN ADMARNAAH\nill work we sent ahead, or evil thought we secretly conceived,\nتَوْبَةَ مَنْ لَا يَنْطَوِي عَلَى رُجُوعٍ اِلَى ذَنْبٍ\nTAWBATA MAN LAA YANTAWEE A'LAA RUJOO'IN ILAA DHANB\nthe repentance of one who does not harbour a return to sin\nوَلَا يَعُودُ بَعْدَهَا فِي خَطِيئَةٍ\nWA LAA YA'OODU BA'DAHAA FEE KHATEE'AH\nand who afterwards will not go back to offense,\nتَوْبَةً نَصُوحاً خَلَصَتْ مِنَ الشَّكِّ وَالِارْتِيَابِ\nTAWBATAN NASOOHAN KHALASAT MINASH SHAKKI WAL IRTIYAAB\nan unswerving repentance rid of doubt and wavering.\nفَتَقَبَّلْهَا مِنَّا، وَارْضَ عَنَّا، وَثَبِّتْنَا عَلَيْهَا\nFATAQABBALHAA MINNAA WARDA A'NNAA WA THABBITNAA A'LAYHAA\nSo accept it from us, be pleased with us, and fix us within it!\nاللَّهُمَّ ارْزُقْنَا خَوْفَ عِقَابِ الْوَعِيدِ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNAA KHAWFA I'QAABIL WA'EED\nGod, provide us with fear of the threatened punishment\nوَشَوْقَ ثَوَابِ الْمَوْعُودِ حَتَّى نَجِدَ لَذَّةَ مَا نَدْعُوكَ بِهٖ\nWA SHAWQA THAWAABIL MAW'OODI HATTAA NAJIDA LADHDHATA MAA NAD'OOKA BIH\nand yearning for the promised reward, so that we may find the pleasure of that for which we supplicate You\nوَكَاْبَةَ مَا نَسْتَجِيرُكَ مِنْهُ\nWA KA'BATA MAA NASTAJEERUKA MINH\nand the sorrow of that from which we seek sanctuary in You!\nوَاجْعَلْنَا عِنْدَكَ مِنَ التَّوَّابِينَ الَّذِينَ اَوْجَبْتَ لَهُمْ مَحَبَّتَكَ\nWAJ'ALNAA I'NDAKA MINAT TAWWAABEENAL LADHEENA AWJABTA LAHUM MAHABBATAK\nAnd place us with You among the repenters, those upon whom You have made Your love obligatory\nوَقَبِلْتَ مِنْهُمْ مُرَاجَعَةَ طَاعَتِكَ، يَا اَعْدَلَ الْعَادِلِينَ\nWA QABILTA MINHUM MURAAJA'ATA TAA'ATIKA YAA A'DALAL A'ADILEEN\nand from whom You have accepted the return to obeying You! O Most Just of the just!\nاللَّهُمَّ تَجَاوَزْ عَنْ اٰبَائِنَا وَاُمَّهَاتِنَا وَاَهْلِ دِينِنَا جَمِيعاً\nALLAAHUMMA TAJAAWAZ A'N AABAA'INAA WA UMMAHAATINAA WA AHLI DEENINAA JAMEE'AA\nO God, show forbearance toward our fathers and our mothers and all the people of our religion,\nمَنْ سَلَفَ مِنْهُمْ وَمَنْ غَبَرَ اِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ\nMAN SALAFA MINHUM WA MAN GHABARA ILAA YAWMIL QIYAAMAH\nthose who have gone and those who will pass by, until the Day of Resurrection!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ نَبِيِّنَا وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN NABIYYINAA WA AALIH\nO God, bless our prophet Muhammad and his Household,\nكَمَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَى مَلَائِكَتِكَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nKAMAA SALLAYTA A'LAA MALAA'IKATIKAL MUQARRABEEN\nas You have blessed Your angels brought nigh,\nوَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA SALLI A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nbless him and his Household,\nكَمَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَى اَنْبِيَائِكَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ\nKAMAA SALLAYTA A'LAA ANBIYAA'IKAL MURSALEEN\nas You have blessed Your prophets sent out,\nوَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ كَمَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَى عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِينَ\nWA SALLI A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE KAMAA SALLAYTA A'LAA I'BAADIKAS SAALIHEEN\nbless him and his Household, as You have blessed Your righteous servants\nوَاَفْضَلَ مِنْ ذَلِكَ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nWA AFDALA MIN DHAALIKA YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nand better than that, O Lord of the worlds!\nصَلَاةً تَبْلُغُنَا بَرَكَتُهَا، وَيَنَالُنَا نَفْعُهَا\nSALAATAN TABLUGHUNAA BARAKATUHAA WA YANAALUNAA NAF'UHAA\na blessing whose benediction will reach us, whose benefit will attain to us,\nوَيُسْتَجَابُ لَهَا دُعَاؤُنَا\nWA YUSTAJAABU LAHAA DU'AA'UNAA\nand through which our supplication may be granted!\nاِنَّكَ اَكْرَمُ مَنْ رُغِبَ اِلَيْهِ\nINNAKA AKRAMU MAN RUGHIBA ILAYH\nYou are the most generous of those who are beseeched,\nوَاَكْفَى مَنْ تُوُكِّلَ عَلَيْهِ\nWA AKFAA MAN TUWUKKILA A'LAYH\nthe most sufficient of those in whom confidence is had,\nوَاَعْطَى مَنْ سُئِلَ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ\nWA A'TAA MAN SU'ILA MIN FADLIH\nthe most bestowing of those from whom bounty is asked,\nوَاَنْتَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ\nWA ANTA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nYou are powerful over everything!",
    "Short Farewell Duas\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ صِيَامِيْ لِشَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN SIYAAMEE LISHAHRI RAMADAAN\nO Allah, (please) do not decide my observance of fasting in this month of Ramadan to be the last of my observance of fasting.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ يَطْلُعَ فَجْرُ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ اِلَّا وَقَدْ غَفَرْتَ لِي\nWA A'OODHU BIKA AN YATLU'A FAJRU HAADHIHIL LAYLATI ILLAA WA QAD GHAFARTA LEE\nI seek Your protection against that this day dawns before You shall forgive me.\nOn the last Friday of Ramazan, bid it farewell with:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ صِيَامِنَا اِيَّاهُ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN SIYAAMINAA IYYAAH\nO Allah, (please) do not make it the last of our fasting in this month\nفَاِنْ جَعَلْتَهٗ فَاجْعَلْنِيْ مَرْحُوْمًا وَلَا تَجْعَلْنِيْ مَحْرُوْمًا\nFA-IN JA'ALTAHOO FAJ'ALNEE MARHOOMAN WA LAA TAJ'ALNEE MAHROOMAA\nbut if You decide so, then (please) make me enjoy (Your) mercy and do not make me deprived (of it).",
    "Ten-Unit Prayer\nPray ten units, two at a time with tashahhud and salam. In each unit, after [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), recite [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) 10 times.\nIn each ruku' and sajdah, recite 10 times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلَآ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَاللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nAll glory be to Allah, all praise be to Allah, there is no god save Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\nAfter the last salam, recite 1,000 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFIRULLAAHA WA ATOOBU ILAYH\nI implore for Allah’s forgiveness and I repent before Him.\nThen go into sajdah and recite:\nيَا حَيُّ يَا قَيُّوْمُ، يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA HAYYU YAA QAYYOOMU YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nO Ever-Alive! O Eternal! O Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nيَا رَحْمٰنَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَرَحِيْمَهُمَا\nYAA RAHMAANAD DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI WA RAHEEMAHUMAA\nO All-beneficent of this world and the Next World and the All-merciful of them!\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ، يَا اِلٰهَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEENA YAA ILAAHAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy! O God of the past and the coming generations!\nاِغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا، وَتَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا صَلَاتَنَا وَصِيَامَنَا وَقِيَامَنَا\nIGHFIR LANAA DHUNOOBANAA WA TAQABBAL MINNAA SALAATANAA WA SIYAAMANAA WA QIYAAMANAA\n(Please) forgive us our sins and accept our prayers, fasting, and worship."
  ],
  "merits": "Sahifa Dua 45: The forty-fifth supplication of al-Sahifah al-Kamilah al-Sajjadiyyah, Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s farewell to the month of Ramadan. Farewell supplications for this night are also mentioned by al-Kulayni, al-Saduq, al-Mufid, al-Tusi, and Sayyid Ibn Tawus - may Allah be pleased with them all.\n\nShort Farewell Duas: Sayyid Ibn Tawus has reported Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying: Whoever bids farewell to the month of Ramadan with the first of these supplicatory prayers, Almighty Allah will forgive him before it dawns and will confer upon him with the bliss of submission before Him (i.e. Almighty Allah).\n\nLast Friday: Sayyid Ibn Tawus and Shaykh al-Saduq have both narrated the following on the authority of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari: I visited the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w.a.) on the last Friday of Ramadan. As he saw me, he said: O Jabir, this is the last Friday of Ramadan. You should thus bid farewell to it by saying the second. Verily, whoever says this supplicatory prayer will win one of the two good things; either attaining the next Ramadan or having the forgiveness and mercy of Almighty Allah.\n\nTen-Unit Prayer: Sayyid Ibn Tawus and al-Kaf'ami have reported the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) as recommending this prayer at the last night of Ramadan. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) then continues, \"I swear by Him Who has sent me with the truth as prophet, Archangel Gabriel has reported to me from Archangel Seraph who directly reports from Almighty Allah that one who offers that prayer will not raise his head from prostration before Almighty Allah forgives him, accepts his acts during the month of Ramadan, and overlooks his sins... etc.\"\n\nIt is worth mentioning that other narrations have confirmed that this prayer is offered at the Night of 'Id al-Fitr (i.e. the first night of Shawwal) with a little difference in the form of the supplicatory prayer."
}
